# Use Bun, not npm

This project uses [Bun](https://bun.sh) as its JavaScript runtime and package manager. Do **not** use npm, npx, yarn, or pnpm in docs, rules, scripts, or agent responses.

## Commands

Run everything from `emu/`:

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Install deps | `bun install` |
| Dev server | `bun dev` |
| Unit tests | `bun test` |
| Mooneye suite | `bun run test:mooneye` |
| Lint | `bun run lint` |
| Format | `bun run format` |

`package.json` scripts already invoke `bun test` internally. Prefer `bun test path/to/file.test.js` for a single file, or `bun run <script>` when a script sets env vars (e.g. `test:mooneye` sets `MOONEYE=1`).

## When writing docs or examples

- ✅ `bun test`, `bun install`, `bun run test:mooneye`
- ❌ `npm test`, `npm install`, `npm run test:mooneye`, `npx`
